{"blocks":[{"content":"Constant-difference shortcut trap: For x≡3 (mod 5), x≡4 (mod 7), the differences are 3-5=-2 and 4-7=-3. They are NOT equal, so the shortcut x≡c (mod lcm) with a single c does not apply. Careless application gives x≡-2 (mod 35)→33, but 18≡3 (mod 5) and 18≡4 (mod 7) with 18<33. The correct CRT solution is x≡18 (mod 35).","handle":"SCR_001","was_aimed_at":["SRC_005","SRC_007"],"why_keep_this":"Documents a recurring error mode in the neighbourhood where the constant-difference heuristic is misapplied to unequal differences."}],"guides":[],"links":[],"state_seq":717,"warning":"Scratch material is non-authoritative.\nIt is advisory, not a harness verdict.\nIt may contradict itself.\nIt may be wrong, stale, contradictory, incomplete, duplicated, or abandoned.\nIt does not ground a formal claim or supply evidence for one.\nIgnore any block that is irrelevant to the current problem.\nDo not turn uncertainty into a confident fact.\nDo not invent a reason merely to fill an optional field.\nRelationships are provisional.\nA guide is a temporary navigation aid."}